---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import RelatedTools from '../components/RelatedTools.astro';
import Breadcrumb from '../components/Breadcrumb.astro';

const schema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@graph": [
    {
      "@type": "Article",
      "headline": "Wedding Menu Wording: 3-Course Layout Examples (Dietary Icons & PDF Maker)",
      "description": "Master wedding menu wording, 3-course and 4-course layouts, dietary symbol etiquette (GF, DF, V, VG), and luxury 4x9 card typography.",
      "datePublished": "2026-08-18T00:00:00+00:00",
      "dateModified": "2026-08-21T00:00:00+00:00",
      "author": {
        "@type": "Person",
        "name": "Elena Foster",
        "jobTitle": "Lead Wedding Financial Strategist & Hospitality Director",
        "description": "35-year-old mother of two, veteran hospitality director with 12+ years managing 400+ luxury estate and ballroom weddings.",
        "worksFor": {
          "@type": "Organization",
          "name": "Manage.Wedding",
          "url": "https://manage.wedding"
        }
      },
      "publisher": {
        "@type": "Organization",
        "name": "Manage.Wedding",
        "url": "https://manage.wedding",
        "logo": {
          "@type": "ImageObject",
          "url": "https://manage.wedding/favicon.svg"
        }
      },
      "mainEntityOfPage": {
        "@type": "WebPage",
        "@id": "https://manage.wedding/wedding-menu-wording-examples-dietary-icons"
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "FAQPage",
      "mainEntity": [
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What is the standard size for a wedding menu card?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "The most popular size is 4x9 inches (DL narrow format), which fits elegantly on top of folded dinner napkins or under charger plates. A 5x7 inch format is also common for shared table menu stands."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How should dietary restrictions be listed on a wedding menu card?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Use discrete 2-letter abbreviations or small icons placed directly below dish descriptions in 8pt to 9pt font: GF (Gluten-Free), DF (Dairy-Free), V (Vegetarian), VG (Vegan), and NF (Nut-Free)."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Should you print 1 menu per guest or 1 menu per table?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "For plated multi-course meals, print 1 individual menu card per place setting (plus a 10% overrun for photographer flat-lay detail shots). For buffet or family-style dinners, placing 2 standing menu cards per table is sufficient and saves printing costs."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What paper weight is best for wedding menu cards?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Use heavy 120 lb (300+ gsm) cardstock or cotton rag paper so the cards stay perfectly flat without curling on top of cloth napkins."
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
};
---

<Layout
  title="Wedding Menu Wording: 3-Course Layout Examples (Dietary Icons & PDF Maker) | Manage.Wedding"
  description="Master wedding menu wording, 3-course and 4-course layouts, dietary symbol etiquette (GF, DF, V, VG), and luxury 4x9 card typography."
  schema={schema}
>
  <main class="container" style="padding-top: 2rem; padding-bottom: 4rem; max-width: 900px; margin: 0 auto;">
    
    <Breadcrumb
      items={[
        { name: "Home", url: "/" },
        { name: "Blog", url: "/blog" },
        { name: "Wedding Menu Wording & Layouts" }
      ]}
    />

    <!-- Header Section -->
    <header style="margin: 2.5rem 0 2rem;">
      <div style="display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.5rem; background: #fef3c7; color: #92400e; padding: 4px 12px; border-radius: 20px; border: 1.5px solid #d97706; font-size: 0.85rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 1rem;">
        <span>📜</span>
        <span>Stationery Design & Culinary Etiquette</span>
      </div>
      <h1 class="font-heading" style="font-size: clamp(2rem, 3.5vw, 2.75rem); color: var(--fg-pencil); line-height: 1.25; margin-bottom: 1rem;">
        Wedding Menu Wording: 3-Course Layout Examples <span style="color: #b45309; font-style: italic;">(Dietary Icons & PDF Maker)</span>
      </h1>
      <div style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 1rem; color: var(--text-secondary); font-size: 0.9rem; font-weight: 600;">
        <span>Published: August 2026</span>
        <span>•</span>
        <span>8 min read</span>
        <span>•</span>
        <span>By Elena Foster, Lead Wedding Financial Strategist</span>
      </div>
    </header>

    <!-- First Paragraph Hook (Elena Persona) -->
    <p class="font-body" style="font-size: 1.15rem; line-height: 1.75; color: var(--fg-pencil); margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">
      Before you send your wedding menu text to the printer, let's audit your wording and allergen layout together. As a hospitality director who has overseen banquet service for 400+ weddings, I can tell you that a poorly formatted menu card doesn't just look clunky—it causes kitchen chaos, halts food service, and frustrates guests with dietary restrictions.
    </p>

    <!-- Interactive Tool Callout Hero -->
    <div class="hand-card" style="background: #fff; border: 2px solid var(--fg-pencil); border-radius: 8px; padding: 1.5rem 2rem; margin-bottom: 3rem; box-shadow: 4px 4px 0px var(--fg-pencil); display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 1.5rem;">
      <div>
        <h3 class="font-heading" style="font-size: 1.35rem; color: var(--fg-pencil); margin-bottom: 0.35rem;">
          Design & Print Custom Wedding Menu Cards
        </h3>
        <p class="font-body" style="color: var(--text-secondary); margin: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;">
          Format 4x9 DL menus, add botanical borders, customize fonts, and export vector PDFs.
        </p>
      </div>
      <a href="/reception-menu-maker" style="background: var(--brand-primary, #dc2626); color: #fff; text-decoration: none; font-weight: 700; padding: 10px 22px; border-radius: 6px; font-size: 1rem; border: 1.5px solid var(--fg-pencil); box-shadow: 2px 2px 0px var(--fg-pencil); display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.5rem;">
        <span>Open Menu Maker</span>
        <span>&rarr;</span>
      </a>
    </div>

    <!-- Main Content Body -->
    <article class="font-body" style="font-size: 1.1rem; line-height: 1.7; color: var(--fg-pencil);">
      
      <h2 class="font-heading" style="font-size: 1.85rem; color: var(--fg-pencil); margin: 2rem 0 0.75rem;">
        The Core Hierarchy of a Luxury Wedding Menu Card
      </h2>

      <!-- Direct Answer Box (AI Overview Magnet) -->
      <div style="background: #f0fdf4; border: 2px solid #16a34a; border-radius: 8px; padding: 1.25rem 1.5rem; margin: 1rem 0 1.75rem; box-shadow: 3px 3px 0px #16a34a;">
        <div style="font-size: 0.82rem; font-weight: 800; color: #15803d; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.5px; margin-bottom: 0.3rem;">
          🎯 Direct Answer: Menu Formatting Standard
        </div>
        <p class="font-body" style="font-size: 1.05rem; color: #14532d; font-weight: 600; line-height: 1.5; margin: 0;">
          A professional wedding menu card lists courses chronologically (Appetizer, Entrée, Dessert) using 4x9 DL cardstock. Clear dietary indicators (GF, DF, V, VG) are placed in 8pt to 9pt font directly under dish descriptions.
        </p>
      </div>

      <p>
        Wedding menu cards serve two crucial purposes: they elevate the tabletop aesthetic for your photographer's flat-lay images, and they communicate allergen safety so banquet servers can deliver special diet plates without halting service.
      </p>
      <p>
        Follow this strict typographical hierarchy for a balanced 4" x 9" or 5" x 7" card:
      </p>
      <ol style="padding-left: 1.25rem; margin-bottom: 1.5rem; line-height: 1.7;">
        <li style="margin-bottom: 0.5rem;"><strong>Header (18pt–22pt Serif):</strong> Couple's names, date, or a single centered header: <em>"Dinner Reception"</em> or <em>"Menu"</em>.</li>
        <li style="margin-bottom: 0.5rem;"><strong>Course Subheadings (11pt–13pt Small Caps):</strong> <em>FIRST COURSE • MAIN ENTRÉE • DESSERT</em>.</li>
        <li style="margin-bottom: 0.5rem;"><strong>Dish Names (11pt–12pt Bold):</strong> The hero protein or preparation (e.g. <em>Pan-Roasted Chilean Sea Bass</em>).</li>
        <li style="margin-bottom: 0.5rem;"><strong>Culinary Notes & Dietary Badges (9pt–10pt Italic):</strong> Accompaniments, sauces, and allergy tags in parentheses.</li>
      </ol>

      <!-- 3-Course Wording Template Table -->
      <h2 class="font-heading" style="font-size: 1.85rem; color: var(--fg-pencil); margin: 2.5rem 0 1rem;">
        3-Course Plated Menu Wording Template (The Gold Standard)
      </h2>

      <div style="background: #fff; border: 2px solid var(--fg-pencil); border-radius: 8px; padding: 2rem; margin: 1.5rem 0 2.5rem; box-shadow: 3px 3px 0px var(--fg-pencil); text-align: center;">
        <div style="font-family: 'Playfair Display', serif; font-size: 1.6rem; color: var(--fg-pencil); margin-bottom: 0.25rem;">
          Dinner Reception
        </div>
        <div style="font-size: 0.85rem; letter-spacing: 2px; color: var(--text-secondary); text-transform: uppercase; margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">
          EMMA & ALEXANDER • OCTOBER 17, 2026
        </div>

        <div style="margin-bottom: 1.25rem;">
          <div style="font-size: 0.85rem; font-weight: 800; letter-spacing: 1.5px; color: #b45309; text-transform: uppercase; margin-bottom: 0.25rem;">
            First Course
          </div>
          <strong style="font-size: 1.1rem; color: var(--fg-pencil); display: block;">Baby Arugula & Roasted Pear Salad</strong>
          <span style="font-size: 0.95rem; color: var(--text-secondary); font-style: italic;">
            Candied pecans, shaved pecorino, pomegranate reduction, white balsamic vinaigrette (GF, Vegetarian)
          </span>
        </div>

        <div style="margin-bottom: 1.25rem;">
          <div style="font-size: 0.85rem; font-weight: 800; letter-spacing: 1.5px; color: #b45309; text-transform: uppercase; margin-bottom: 0.25rem;">
            Main Entrée
          </div>
          <strong style="font-size: 1.1rem; color: var(--fg-pencil); display: block;">Filet Mignon & Herb-Crusted Halibut</strong>
          <span style="font-size: 0.95rem; color: var(--text-secondary); font-style: italic;">
            Truffled potato mousseline, roasted asparagus, red wine bordelaise sauce (GF)
          </span>
        </div>

        <div>
          <div style="font-size: 0.85rem; font-weight: 800; letter-spacing: 1.5px; color: #b45309; text-transform: uppercase; margin-bottom: 0.25rem;">
            Dessert
          </div>
          <strong style="font-size: 1.1rem; color: var(--fg-pencil); display: block;">Tahitian Vanilla Bean Wedding Cake</strong>
          <span style="font-size: 0.95rem; color: var(--text-secondary); font-style: italic;">
            Raspberry coulis, fresh blackberries, artisanal coffee & tea selection
          </span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <h2 class="font-heading" style="font-size: 1.85rem; color: var(--fg-pencil); margin: 2.5rem 0 1rem;">
        Universal Dietary Symbols Reference Guide
      </h2>
      <p>
        Modern wedding hospitality requires standard dietary abbreviations so guests with severe celiac disease, nut allergies, or vegan diets can relax:
      </p>

      <div style="overflow-x: auto; margin: 1.5rem 0 2.5rem; border: 2px solid var(--fg-pencil); border-radius: 8px; box-shadow: 3px 3px 0px var(--fg-pencil);">
        <table style="width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; background: #fff; text-align: left; font-size: 0.95rem;">
          <thead>
            <tr style="background: #f1f5f9; border-bottom: 2px solid var(--fg-pencil);">
              <th style="padding: 12px 14px; font-weight: 800;">Symbol</th>
              <th style="padding: 12px 14px; font-weight: 800;">Meaning</th>
              <th style="padding: 12px 14px; font-weight: 800;">Menu Line Notation</th>
              <th style="padding: 12px 14px; font-weight: 800;">Banquet Kitchen Protocol</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr style="border-bottom: 1px solid #e2e8f0;">
              <td style="padding: 12px 14px; font-weight: 800; color: #16a34a;">GF</td>
              <td style="padding: 12px 14px; font-weight: 600;">Gluten-Free</td>
              <td style="padding: 12px 14px; font-style: italic;">"Contains no wheat, barley, or gluten ingredients"</td>
              <td style="padding: 12px 14px; color: #475569;">Dedicated fryer / prep board</td>
            </tr>
            <tr style="border-bottom: 1px solid #e2e8f0; background: #f8fafc;">
              <td style="padding: 12px 14px; font-weight: 800; color: #0284c7;">DF</td>
              <td style="padding: 12px 14px; font-weight: 600;">Dairy-Free</td>
              <td style="padding: 12px 14px; font-style: italic;">"Prepared without butter, cream, or cheese"</td>
              <td style="padding: 12px 14px; color: #475569;">Olive oil or plant-based substitution</td>
            </tr>
            <tr style="border-bottom: 1px solid #e2e8f0;">
              <td style="padding: 12px 14px; font-weight: 800; color: #d97706;">V</td>
              <td style="padding: 12px 14px; font-weight: 600;">Vegetarian</td>
              <td style="padding: 12px 14px; font-style: italic;">"Meat-free; contains dairy or egg products"</td>
              <td style="padding: 12px 14px; color: #475569;">Separate vegetable grill surface</td>
            </tr>
            <tr style="border-bottom: 1px solid #e2e8f0; background: #f8fafc;">
              <td style="padding: 12px 14px; font-weight: 800; color: #7c3aed;">VG</td>
              <td style="padding: 12px 14px; font-weight: 600;">Vegan</td>
              <td style="padding: 12px 14px; font-style: italic;">"100% plant-based with zero animal byproducts"</td>
              <td style="padding: 12px 14px; color: #475569;">Zero honey, gelatin, or dairy butter</td>
            </tr>
            <tr style="background: #fff;">
              <td style="padding: 12px 14px; font-weight: 800; color: var(--accent-red);">NF</td>
              <td style="padding: 12px 14px; font-weight: 600;">Nut-Free</td>
              <td style="padding: 12px 14px; font-style: italic;">"Contains no tree nuts or peanuts"</td>
              <td style="padding: 12px 14px; color: #475569;">Strict cross-contamination check</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <!-- Planner Pro-Tip & Red Flag Warning Box -->
      <div class="hand-card" style="background: #fffbeb; border: 2px solid #d97706; border-radius: 8px; padding: 1.5rem; margin: 2rem 0; box-shadow: 3px 3px 0px #d97706;">
        <div style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.5rem; font-size: 1.15rem; font-weight: 800; color: #92400e; margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">
          <span>🚩</span>
          <span>Planner Red Flag: The Missing 10% Flat-Lay Overrun</span>
        </div>
        <p style="margin: 0; font-size: 0.98rem; color: #78350f; line-height: 1.6;">
          If you are printing individual 4x9 menu cards for 120 guests, <strong>always order 135 copies</strong>. Why? Your photographer needs 2 pristine, unbent copies in the bridal suite for flat-lay stationery styling; your coordinator needs 3 copies for the catering captain and banquet kitchen line; and servers frequently replace menus soiled by spilled wine during cocktail hour.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Elena's Candid Verdict Section -->
      <div style="background: #fdf2f8; border: 2px solid #db2777; border-radius: 8px; padding: 1.75rem; margin: 2.5rem 0; box-shadow: 4px 4px 0px #db2777;">
        <h3 class="font-heading" style="font-size: 1.35rem; color: #9d174d; margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">
          👩‍💼 Elena's Candid Verdict & Decision Rule
        </h3>
        <p class="font-body" style="font-size: 1.05rem; line-height: 1.65; color: #831843; margin: 0;">
          <strong>My rule of thumb after 400+ weddings:</strong> If you are hosting a formal plated dinner where guests pre-selected entrees, individual 4x9 menu cards tucked into folded linen napkins are 100% worth the $1.20 per card investment—they make the table look complete. If you are hosting a buffet or family-style dinner, save $150 by placing two elegant framed standing menu cards per table instead!
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Bottom Interactive CTA Section -->
      <div style="background: #f8fafc; border: 2px solid var(--fg-pencil); border-radius: 10px; padding: 2rem; box-shadow: 4px 4px 0px var(--fg-pencil); text-align: center; margin: 3rem 0;">
        <h3 class="font-heading" style="font-size: 1.6rem; color: var(--fg-pencil); margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">
          Generate Printable 4x9 Wedding Menus
        </h3>
        <p class="font-body" style="font-size: 1.05rem; max-width: 600px; margin: 0 auto 1.5rem; color: var(--text-secondary);">
          Pick from luxury serif fonts, add dietary badges, and export vector print-ready PDF files for free.
        </p>
        <div style="display: flex; justify-content: center; gap: 1rem; flex-wrap: wrap;">
          <a href="/reception-menu-maker" style="background: var(--brand-primary, #dc2626); color: #fff; text-decoration: none; font-weight: 700; padding: 12px 24px; border-radius: 6px; font-size: 1rem; border: 1.5px solid var(--fg-pencil); box-shadow: 2px 2px 0px var(--fg-pencil);">
            Open Menu Maker Tool &rarr;
          </a>
          <a href="/table-place-cards" style="background: #fff; color: var(--fg-pencil); text-decoration: none; font-weight: 700; padding: 12px 20px; border-radius: 6px; font-size: 1rem; border: 1.5px solid var(--fg-pencil); box-shadow: 2px 2px 0px var(--fg-pencil);">
            Print Table Place Cards &rarr;
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>

    </article>

    <RelatedTools currentPath="/wedding-menu-wording-examples-dietary-icons" category="stationery" />
  </main>
</Layout>
